## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine TLS edge proxying with per-tenant feature gates loaded from a daemon-managed config source. It also checks bootstrap discipline in a two-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Configs for runtime config
- TLS termination at Nginx edge proxy
- Per-tenant feature gates in a small API
- Simple bootstrap for tenants and flags

## Code Example
```javascript
const fs = require('fs');
const yaml = require('js-yaml');
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
let flags = {};
function loadFlags() {
  const txt = fs.readFileSync('/etc/feature-flags.yaml','utf8');
  flags = yaml.load(txt) || {};
}
loadFlags();
app.get('/health-quiz', (req, res) => {
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  if (tenant && flags[tenant] && flags[tenant].enabled) res.sendStatus(200);
  else res.sendStatus(403);
});
app.listen(3000);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this gating with CI and two data centers?
- What are failure modes if the config-loader container is unavailable?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to drive feature-flag configurations from Docker Configs in a multi-DC setup, plus per-tenant routing and safe fallbacks.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Configs for per-tenant flags
- X-Tenant header routing and fallback strategies
- In-process caching with TTL and config-driven feature gates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js Express snippet to load tenant flags from docker config mounted at /config
app.use((req,res,next)=>{
  const t = req.header('X-Tenant');
  let flags = cache.get(t);
  if(!flags){
    try{
      const raw = fs.readFileSync(`/config/feature-flags-${t}.json`, 'utf8');
      flags = JSON.parse(raw);
      cache.set(t, flags);
    }catch(e){
      flags = globalDefaults;
    }
  }
  req.flags = flags;
  next();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you invalidate tenant flag cache when the Docker Config changes without restarting the API?
- How would you test this across two DCs with Traefik and simulate Config updates?
